Why not the repository's AGPL-3.0: WordPress itself is GPLv2-or-later and its plugin directory asks
for a GPLv2-compatible licence; this connector talks to a prepress-open instance over HTTP and ships
none of the AGPL-licensed engine, so it can carry WordPress's own licence. The engine stays AGPL-3.0.
